__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# v0.4 real-plan dataset: raw customer PDFs and the pseudonym<->filename
# mapping are never committed (title blocks carry real names/addresses/
# companies) -- only the derived, pseudonymous annotation_dataset/ is.
# See docs/v04-dataset-report.md's privacy-audit section.
data/dev_plans_v04/raw/
data/dev_plans_v04/id_mapping.LOCAL_ONLY.json
# Defense-in-depth: a crashed pipeline run can leave one of these behind
# with a plan's UNFILTERED raw legend text (taxonomy.py's privacy filter
# only runs when run_v04_pipeline.py reads and aggregates it normally) --
# never committed even if a crash leaves one on disk.
data/dev_plans_v04/annotation_dataset/_worker_*.tmp.json
# Legend + vector-geometry structural benchmark (docs/v04-legend-structural-benchmark-report.md):
# predictions.json holds full per-candidate bbox/page detail for 648
# schema-area symbols; it adds nothing beyond what the report already
# summarizes, so it stays local (re-creatable any time by re-running
# scripts/legend_benchmark_phaseA_predict.py against the same 5 raw PDFs).
# freeze_manifest.json (the SHA-256 + holdout audit) and
# phaseC_score_report.json (the full scoring detail) are small and kept.
data/dev_plans_v04/legend_structural_benchmark/predictions.json
